{"id":128,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield"],"text":"The Tauros of the Galar region are volatile in nature, and they won’t allow people to ride on their backs."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"When Tauros begins whipping itself with its tails, it’s a warning that the Pokémon is about to charge with astounding speed."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!","Yellow"],"text":"A rowdy Pokémon with a lot of stamina. Once running, it won’t stop until it hits something."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"The climate seems to be related to the reason Tauros in Alola are a little calmer than those in other regions."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"They live in groups. The one with the longest, thickest, and most-scarred horns is the boss of the herd."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"Although it’s known to be a fierce Pokémon, Tauros in the Alola region are said to possess a measure of calmness."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Historically, people in areas all over the world have ridden Tauros, but the practice is said to have started in Alola."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Omega Ruby","Sapphire","Ruby"],"text":"This Pokémon is not satisfied unless it is rampaging at all times. If there is no opponent for Tauros to battle, it will charge at thick trees and knock them down to calm itself."},{"games":["Y","FireRed"],"text":"When it is about to tackle, it whips its body repeatedly with its three long tails."},{"games":["X","SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"After heightening its will to fight by whipping itself with its three tails, it charges at full speed."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"Once it takes aim at its foe, it makes a headlong charge. It is famous for its violent nature."},{"games":["HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"They fight each other by locking horns. The herd’s protector takes pride in its battle-scarred horns."},{"games":["LeafGreen","Blue","Red"],"text":"When it targets an enemy, it charges furiously while whipping its body with its long tails."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"It is not satisfied unless it is rampaging at all times. If there is no opponent for TAUROS to battle, it will charge at thick trees and knock them down to calm itself."},{"games":["Crystal"],"text":"These violent POKéMON fight with other members of their herd in order to prove their strength."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Intimidate","hidden":false,"description":"When the Pokémon enters a battle, it intimidates opposing Pokémon and makes them cower, lowering their Attack stats."},{"name":"Anger Point","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon is angered when it takes a critical hit, and that maxes its Attack stat."},{"name":"Sheer Force","hidden":true,"description":"Removes any additional effects from the Pokémon's moves, but increases the moves' power."}],"eggGroups":["Field"],"genderRate":0,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"slow","habitat":"grassland","color":"Brown","shape":"Quadruped","evolution":{"id":128,"name":"Tauros","condition":null,"children":[]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,33],[1,39],[5,526],[10,371],[15,372],[20,30],[25,184],[30,428],[35,873],[40,156],[45,207],[50,37],[55,38],[60,416]],"machine":[59,34,523,370,174,91,38,89,283,203,263,126,53,416,270,667,63,58,196,442,808,200,182,240,156,179,157,317,201,184,247,214,684,76,707,444,164,241,57,36,851,168,675,87,85,885,528,428],"egg":[174,283],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"me4-96","name":"Tauros","set":"Chaos Rising","date":"2026-05-22","rarity":"Illustration Rare","number":"96","artist":"Tsuyoshi Nagano","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me4-96/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me4-96/large"},{"id":"me4-69","name":"Tauros","set":"Chaos Rising","date":"2026-05-22","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"69","artist":"Satoshi Ito","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me4-69/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me4-69/large"},{"id":"me2-48","name":"Paldean Tauros","set":"Phantasmal Flames","d